@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# Frozen MeSH 2026 exact-resolution snapshot
+
+## Status and scope
+
+This is a separately versioned terminology configuration, not a rewrite of the v21 conversion engine. The 620-key corpus cache remains at `resources/mesh_resolution_cache_v20_v1_YW_18092026.json`, with SHA-256 `a975dee7b863d6bd74199ded85ffe9f36cb44963e3f897fe5c9c8a3e923e91f1`. It has not been extended, merged with the new data, or overwritten. Its retention is provenance preservation, not proof that it was the exact configuration of a historical benchmark run.
+
+The new resources contain complete exact-label indexes of the English 2026 Descriptor, Supplementary Concept Record (SCR), and Qualifier XML files downloaded from NLM. They are not a full-text export of scope notes, history notes, or tree descriptions. The **browser converter consumes the descriptor resource only**. SCRs and qualifiers are packaged separately and are not silently reclassified as `[mh]` descriptors or given unapproved conversion rules.
+
+| Resource | Records | Distinct normalised labels within resource |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Descriptors | 31,110 | 267,012 |
+| Supplementary concepts | 324,046 | 729,017 |
+| Qualifiers | 76 | 303 |
+
+The descriptor resource contains 30,512 topical descriptors, 194 publication types, 2 check tags and 402 geographical descriptors. Every canonical descriptor name and every `ConceptList/Concept/TermList/Term/String` is indexed. No API search-result limit or corpus-selected heading list is used.
+
+## Authoritative inputs and freezing
+
+See `resources/mesh2026_source_lock_v1_YW_18092026.json`. It records the original URLs, retrieval times, HTTP Last-Modified values, sizes and SHA-256 hashes. All three downloaded files reported Last-Modified on 12 August 2026. They were acquired on 18 September 2026. A frozen snapshot is not a claim to reflect the latest daily NLM update.
+
+NLM XML sources:
+
+- https://nlmpubs.nlm.nih.gov/projects/mesh/MESH_FILES/xmlmesh/desc2026.gz
+- https://nlmpubs.nlm.nih.gov/projects/mesh/MESH_FILES/xmlmesh/supp2026.gz
+- https://nlmpubs.nlm.nih.gov/projects/mesh/MESH_FILES/xmlmesh/qual2026.xml
+
+The builder checks all input byte hashes and sizes, English root elements, the 2026 DTD reference, unique record identities, supported record classes, minimum full-file coverage and referential integrity of direct PA targets. It uses streaming XML parsing without downloading or executing the external DTD. A changed source fails the hash lock rather than silently creating a new snapshot under the same identity.
+
+Rebuild from the archived source files, from repository root:
+
+```powershell
+python scripts/build_mesh_2026_snapshot_v1_YW_18092026.py `
+  --source-dir "C:\path\to\archived_NLM_sources" `
+  --source-lock resources/mesh2026_source_lock_v1_YW_18092026.json `
+  --output-dir resources/mesh2026
+```
+
+JSON uses sorted keys, UTF-8 and LF. Gzip uses an empty filename and a zero timestamp. The source lock fixes the acquisition timestamp, so repeated builds do not invent new provenance. The manifest records output hashes, counts, the builder hash and the comparison with the preserved cache.
+
+## Exact matching and ambiguity
+
+The browser adapter delegates typography, whitespace and case normalisation to the unchanged reference engine. It applies the ten existing reviewed historical aliases, then exact preferred-label matching, then exact entry-term matching. Multiple occurrences of a term within one descriptor do not manufacture ambiguity; distinct candidate descriptor IDs remain distinct. No fuzzy search, punctuation guessing, token reordering, history-note inference, nearest-term mapping, or ad-hoc external-benchmark alias has been added.
+
+Ambiguity remains explicitly supported and tested, although the supplied English 2026 descriptor index contains no ambiguous normalised preferred or entry keys. Missing or ambiguous labels use the existing audited source-heading fallback. Completeness of the current vocabulary does not imply that misspellings or every historical Ovid expression can be resolved.
+
+## Pharmacological-action direction
+
+The PA flag means **this descriptor is the target of a direct pharmacological-action relation from a substance**, not that the descriptor is a chemical with its own actions. Direct edges are collected from both Descriptor and SCR XML. The result contains 567 PA targets, including 105 targets seen only in SCR records. The separate `pa2026.xml` expansion file is deliberately not used because it also includes selected ancestors, unlike the reference resolver's direct-edge query with inference disabled.
+
+The conversion engine still adds `[pa]` only for an explicitly exploded applicable heading. Ordinary headings do not acquire an extra `[pa]` branch merely because metadata are available.
+
+## Browser packaging
+
+The descriptor JSON is 12,722,891 bytes, or 2,532,483 bytes in its frozen gzip form. The browser normally requests the gzip asset from the same static host and decompresses it locally. Both compressed and decompressed hashes are checked. An uncompressed same-origin asset is retained for environments without `DecompressionStream`. No external terminology service or new backend is introduced.
+
+The runtime manifest identifies the selected terminology profile, snapshot ID, frozen timestamp, source files, data hashes, descriptor count, exact-label count and unchanged Python reference hashes. The UI distinguishes a complete descriptor snapshot from the 620-key corpus cache. Only public terminology is memoised; user strategies and results are not retained in that cache.
+
+From repository root, select the preserved profile explicitly for a build:
+
+```powershell
+$env:MESH_TERMINOLOGY_PROFILE = "corpus-620"
+cd browser
+npm run build
+```
+
+Select the candidate full descriptor profile:
+
+```powershell
+$env:MESH_TERMINOLOGY_PROFILE = "mesh2026-complete"
+cd browser
+npm run build
+```
+
+In this candidate branch the default profile is `mesh2026-complete`. Nothing changes on the live Pages site until a reviewed change is merged and deployed.
+
+## Relationship to the corpus and reported evaluation
+
+All 620 existing keys resolve to the same descriptor ID, canonical label, record class, PA flag and match type in the new snapshot. This does **not** imply that every complete strategy has identical output: a previously uncached heading can now resolve and change an audit event, canonical label, field or PA branch. Any results produced under the new terminology profile must be labelled as such rather than retroactively substituted for the original evaluation.
+
